@startuml tga-profiling-sequence
!include ../../theme.iuml

title Check TGA & set up frontend profiling — you, teamscale-mcp & teamscale-docs-mcp

actor "You" as U
participant "Claude" as C
participant "teamscale-docs-mcp" as D
participant "teamscale-mcp" as T

legend top right
|= color |= source |
|<back:#1971c2>    </back>| teamscale-docs-mcp — concepts & how-tos |
|<back:#e8590c>    </back>| teamscale-mcp — live project data |
endlegend

autonumber

== Learn the concept (docs) ==
U -> C : what is TGA in Teamscale?
C -[#1971c2]> D : list_documentation / get_documentation_page(test-gap analysis)
D --[#1971c2]> C : Test Gap Analysis — changed vs. tested code
C --> U : explanation of TGA

== Pull the data (teamscale) ==
U -> C : show TGA for my "traureise" project
C -[#e8590c]> T : getAllProjectIds() -> getProject() -> getTgaPercentage()
T --[#e8590c]> C : 0% (suspicious)

== Diagnose the 0% (teamscale) ==
U -> C : coverage definitely exists
C -[#e8590c]> T : getTgaPercentage(all-partitions, churn), getAllBaselines()
T --[#e8590c]> C : no baselines -> empty change window
C -[#e8590c]> T : getTgaPercentage(baseline main:1 -> HEAD)
T --[#e8590c]> C : ~22% test gap
note over C #D3F9D8
  <b>Relate:</b> the 0% wasn't a coverage problem —
  TGA needs a baseline to define the change window
end note

== Localize the gap (teamscale) ==
U -> C : which methods make up the 22%?
C -[#e8590c]> T : getDeltaAffectedFiles(main:1 -> HEAD)
C -[#e8590c]> T : getTgaPercentage(uniform-path = per directory / file)
T --[#e8590c]> C : frontend/src 100%, backend utils.py & login.py
note over C, T #FFF3BF
  <b>Where the gap lives</b>
  frontend/src ....... 100% (no coverage mapped)
  backend/app ........ 13% (utils.py, routes/utils.py, login.py)
  crud / core / most routes .. 0% (covered)
end note

== Act on it (docs how-to) ==
U -> C : help me set up frontend coverage profiling
C -[#1971c2]> D : get_documentation_page(javascript profiler / setup how-to)
D --[#1971c2]> C : instrumenter + collector steps, source maps, CSP
C --> U : runbook — JS Profiler (Playwright E2E) + Vitest (unit)

@enduml
